 1074 "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nY∨(Y∧Z)≡Y.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $Y.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Z∧Y)∨Y & ≡Y∨(Z∧Y) \\\\  & ≡Y∨(Y∧Z) \\\\  & ≡Y.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is *not* logically equivalent to $Y.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement III is *not* logically equivalent to $Y.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572685 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572685 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572685 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572685 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $H?$\n\nI. $(¬K∧H)∨H$\n\nII. $(H∨¬K)∨H$\n\nIII. $H∨(¬K∧H)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572685 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3b3dcd41-a4d5-5b14-ab14-5e50dc512f91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572685 #edb/ref 1074 "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nH∨(H∧¬K)≡H.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $H.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(¬K∧H)∨H & ≡H∨(¬K∧H) \\\\  & ≡H∨(H∧¬K) \\\\  & ≡H.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is *not* logically equivalent to $H.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $H.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H∨(¬K∧H) & ≡H∨(H∧¬K) \\\\  & ≡H.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572701 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572701 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81715" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572701 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1